Next, roughly by value / effort
-------------------------------
1. Credential storage via `keyring` (or an age/sops-encrypted env file), so
   unattended runs stop needing SYSNET_PASS in the environment.
2. ERS/BOSS structured parsers, mirroring features/voss_parsers.py, so the
   validator names ports and VLANs on ERS instead of falling back to a raw
   output diff. Fixtures live in switch-migrator's tests/fixtures/ers/.
3. Fleet audit report: fan out across the inventory, render one HTML or
   Markdown health report (ports, neighbours, config drift) per run.
4. Real SNMP support via pysnmp (walk + table getters), replacing the
   hand-rolled BER encoder in features/ip_hardware.py.
5. Offline/replay mode: run every tool against saved raw captures instead of
   a device, the way switch-migrator's --offline works. The snapshots the
   validator already writes are most of the raw material.
6. Bundled OUI file for offline MAC vendor lookup (the old macvendors.co
   tool was removed — the API now needs a key).
